s established the Interagency Employee Benefit Council.\n1— 102. The Council shall be composed of the following, or their representa­\ntives:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101 (lead-in)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Secretary of the Treasury.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(a)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Attorney General.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(b)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Secretary of Commerce.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(c)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) The Secretary of Labor.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(d)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) The Secretary of Health and Human Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(e)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) The Director of the Office of Management and Budget.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(f)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(g) The Administrator of the Small Business Administration.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(g)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(g)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(h) The Chairman of the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(h)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(h)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(i) The Executive Director of the President’s Commission on Pension Policy.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-101(i)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-101(i)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-103. The following, or their designated representatives, are invited to partici­\npate in the activities of the Council:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-103 (lead-in)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-103","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Federal Trade Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-103(a)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-103(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Securities and Exchange Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-103(b)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-103(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The National Labor Relations Board.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-103(c)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-103(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Any other Executive agencies the Council invites.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-103(d)","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-103(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-104. The Secretary of Labor shall be the Chairman of the Council.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-104","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-104","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-2. F u n c tio n s o f  t h e  C o u n cil.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-2","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-201. The Council shall assist in interagency coordination of proposals \naffecting employee benefits under ERISA. It shall identify the potential eco­\nnomic consequences of those proposals for ERISA participants.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-201","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-201","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-202. The Council shall develop comprehensive long-term and short-term \npolicies applicable to the plans covered by ERISA. The Council shall identify \nand coordinate research into employee benefit issues affecting ERISA-covered \nemployees, into the economic effects of private pensions, and into the effec­\ntiveness of ERISA.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-202","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-202","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-203. The Council shall develop effective policy approaches to a comprehen­\nsive information-sharing program among ERISA agencies, including develop­\nment of a common or coordinated data base, data use, and publications. The \nCouncil shall develop a program for the use of common facilities and a \ncommon information system.\n\n=== PDF page 10 of 288 ===\n2314 Federal Register /  Vol. 46, No. 6 /  Friday, January 9, 1981 /  Presidential Documents\n1-204. The Council shall identify inconsistencies in the operation of programs \nunder ERISA . It shall recom m end to the President w ays to reduce or eliminate \nthose inconsistencies.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-203","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-203","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-205. W here feasible, the Council should coordinate public participation \nthrough public hearingsjon governm ent-w ide ER ISA -related programs.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-205","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-205","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-206. The Council shall establish and m aintain a m echanism  to evaluate the \neffectiveness of the overall ER ISA  program.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-206","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-206","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-207. The Council shall submit annually to the President a summary report of \nsignificant ERISA -related achievem ents of the m em ber agencies.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-207","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-207","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-3. A d m in is tr a tiv e  P r o v is io n s .","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-3","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12262#sec1-3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-301. The Council shall m eet at le ast once each quarter.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 2313, PDF pages 9-10; Sec. 1-301","sha256":"400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/conten